"""One shared decision page based on the existing evidence, with no new test claims."""
def add_validation_decision(d,P,new_page,para,table,picture):
 if not (P/'validation-decision/decision.json').exists():return
 new_page(d,'Software validation decision')
 para(d,'25 October 2026. Neither product has passed full software validation. We have completed this review of the saved evidence. Several tests and inputs remain missing or unresolved, so the review does not approve a finished product. We reused the existing records and ran no new simulation campaign for this decision.')
 table(d,['Product','Current decision'],[['SoftSpace','Not approved. Joint strength remains unresolved and the local correction has not been validated in the complete headset.'],['SoftSpace Flex','Not approved. Exact Sony mounting geometry and host specific fit and sound results remain unverified.']],[1.6,5.3])
 para(d,'What is established: CAD candidates and calculation records exist. Two V26A reference fields passed their numerical consistency checks. V26B passed 25 local rigid folding samples and two stop queries. A still failed tongue stress and folding checks; B has no accepted strength field. These results do not prove wearer comfort, sound reduction, Sony compatibility or durability.')
 table(d,['Open requirement','What must change before it can close'],[['Joint strength and assembly','A reliably solved motion compatible design with actual hardware loads tolerances and full assembly checks'],['Cushion contact','Selected foam loading and unloading curves cover behaviour seams friction and head geometry'],['Sony mounting','Traceable skirt groove and carrier dimensions and tolerances'],['Sound heat and durability','Defined performance requirements complete product models and qualified material and assembly inputs'],['Comfort and sensory acceptance','Voluntary representative wearer evaluation including autistic users']],[2.05,4.85])
 para(d,'The requirements file separates failed calculations, missing inputs and checks that need people. Repeating assumed simulations cannot establish missing material properties or exact mounting dimensions. We have not loosened any test limit or treated an incomplete solver run as a pass. Testing every imaginable material or headphone is not a finite requirement; actual grades supported models and operating conditions must be defined.')
 para(d,'This closes the evidence review only. It does not complete the outstanding software tests or release either design for manufacture. Further work should address a named open requirement with a changed design or qualified new input. The detailed evidence index and remaining requirements are in the validation decision package.')
